# virtual-sites-spread.test on a GPU (D298): the derived
# spreading against the written one, three OPC waters with Amber's extra
# point, in double precision (forces within 1e-12 of the largest) and in
# mixed precision (within 1e-6; measured 6.7e-8 here, 9e-8 on alanine
# dipeptide in 387 OPC waters), the columns of the energy file to 1e-5
# in double and 1e-4 in mixed (measured 1.1e-5 over the 50 steps).
#
# REQUIRES: cuda
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/double %t/mixed
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/opc/three.prmtop %S/Inputs/opc/three.inpcrd %t/double
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/opc/three.prmtop %S/Inputs/opc/three.inpcrd %t/mixed
# RUN: sed -n '/^#--- run.toml/,/^#--- end/p' %S/virtual-sites.test | sed '1d;$d' \
# RUN:   | sed -e 's/^steps .*/steps = 50/' -e 's/^energy_interval .*/energy_interval = 1/' \
# RUN:   > %t/run.toml
# RUN: cp %t/run.toml %t/double/run.toml && cp %t/run.toml %t/mixed/run.toml
# RUN: printf '\n[execution]\ntarget = "GPU"\nprecision = "DOUBLE"\n' >> %t/double/run.toml
# RUN: printf '\n[execution]\ntarget = "GPU"\nprecision = "MIXED"\n' >> %t/mixed/run.toml
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/compare_site_spread.py mdir %t/double/run.toml 1e-12 1e-5 \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/compare_site_spread.py mdir %t/mixed/run.toml 1e-6 1e-4 \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
#
# CHECK: forces: 12 particles
# CHECK: energy columns: 51 rows
# CHECK: spread ok
